{"t":1792372617048,"type":"FeatureCollection","features":[{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.72c179377d9c445b84dda28dcc1439bd8286059f.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[144.31,12.98],[144.46,13.52],[144.72,14.07],[145.66,13.58],[145.56,13.28],[145.35,12.93],[145.1,12.69],[144.95,12.61],[144.31,12.98]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.72c179377d9c445b84dda28dcc1439bd8286059f.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.72c179377d9c445b84dda28dcc1439bd8286059f.001.1","areaDesc":"Guam Coastal Waters; Rota Coastal Waters","geocode":{"SAME":["065151","065152"],"UGC":["PMZ151","PMZ152"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/forecast/PMZ151","https://api.weather.gov/zones/forecast/PMZ152"],"references":[],"sent":"2026-10-19T11:12:00+10:00","effective":"2026-10-19T11:09:00+10:00","onset":"2026-10-19T11:12:00+10:00","expires":"2026-10-19T12:00:00+10:00","ends":"2026-10-19T12:00:00+10:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Alert","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Special Marine Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Tiyan GU","headline":"Special Marine Warning issued October 19 at 11:09AM ChST until October 19 at 12:00PM ChST by NWS Tiyan GU","description":"SMWGUM\n\nTHE NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE IN TIYAN GUAM HAS ISSUED A\n\n* SPECIAL MARINE WARNING FOR...\nGUAM COASTAL WATERS...\n\n* UNTIL NOON CHST.\n\n* AT 1109 AM CHST...A STRONG THUNDERSTORM WAS LOCATED OVER\nSOUTHEAST GUAM COASTAL WATERS, MOVING NORTH AT 35 KNOTS.\n\nHAZARD...WIND GUSTS 34 KNOTS OR GREATER.\n\nSOURCE...RADAR.\n\nIMPACT...SMALL CRAFT COULD BE DAMAGED IN BRIEFLY HIGHER WINDS\nAND SUDDENLY HIGHER WAVES.\n\n* THE STRONG THUNDERSTORM WILL REMAIN OVER MAINLY OPEN WATERS.","instruction":"MOVE TO SAFE HARBOR UNTIL HAZARDOUS WEATHER PASSES.\n\nMOVE TO SAFE HARBOR IMMEDIATELY AS GUSTY WINDS AND HIGH WAVES ARE\nEXPECTED.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["SMWGUM"],"WMOidentifier":["WHMY50 PGUM 190112"],"eventMotionDescription":["2026-10-19T01:09:00-00:00...storm...186DEG...43KT...12.95,144.84"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.PGUM.MA.W.0036.261019T0112Z-261019T0200Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-10-19T12:00:00+10:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["SMW"],"NationalWeatherService":["MAW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ae8e54e11e9105fc7e4866ee9a809176c3d3d8bf.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-81.5,29.08],[-81.69,29.32],[-81.57,29.35],[-81.42,29.1],[-81.5,29.08]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ae8e54e11e9105fc7e4866ee9a809176c3d3d8bf.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ae8e54e11e9105fc7e4866ee9a809176c3d3d8bf.001.1","areaDesc":"Lake, FL; Volusia, FL","geocode":{"SAME":["012069","012127"],"UGC":["FLC069","FLC127"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/FLC069","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/FLC127"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e267454960d05028ffb17d918dbfe239270f59aa.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e267454960d05028ffb17d918dbfe239270f59aa.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-10-18T09:11:00-04:00"}],"sent":"2026-10-18T20:58:00-04:00","effective":"2026-10-18T20:58:00-04:00","onset":"2026-10-18T20:58:00-04:00","expires":"2026-10-19T12:00:00-04:00","ends":null,"status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Melbourne FL","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 18 at 8:58PM EDT by NWS Melbourne FL","description":"...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Florida...\n\nSt Johns River Near Astor affecting Volusia and Lake Counties.\n\n.Northeast winds are causing river levels on the St Johns at Astor to\nrise through Minor Flood Stage. The river is forecast to reach\nModerate Flood Stage early Monday, and remain in this stage through\nthe end of this week.\n\nFor the St. Johns River...including Astor...Moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHERE...St Johns River near Astor.\n\n* WHEN...Until further notice.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 2.8 feet, Docks and boat ramps covered at South Moon\nFish Camp and approaching sea wall at Blair's Jungle Den. Water\napproaching sites closest to the river at Fish Tales RV Resort and\nAstor Landing Campground. Portion of Clair Street covered by river\nwater south of the Butler Boat Ramp. Docks underwater at the Astor\nBridge Marina and along Riveredge Drive. Portions of Fox Road are\ncovered with water nearest to the river. Acorn, Hazelnut and Redbud\nroads are underwater with yards inundated. At 3.0 feet, Water\napproaches or may enter lowest homes on or near Wildhog Road and\nnearby canals. Flooding reaches the parking lot of the Juno Trail\nApartments. Flooding on portions of Alligator Road and Holiday\nRoad. Lowest lying yards along Blue Creek are flooded. Roads at\nAstor Landing Campground and Lake Dexter Boat Ramp begin to flood.\nWater enters lower homes closest to the river on McPherson Lane. At\n3.5 feet, Canals have overflowed into yards. Homes on or near\nWildhog, Bonnet and Snail roads become inaccessible with several\ninches of water inside homes along the river and canals. Docks at\nAstor Bridge marina and throughout Astor are completely submerged.\nBartram Rd and Holiday Circle are inaccessible with yards\ncompletely submerged. Clair Street is inaccessible. Roads flooded\nin South Moon Fish Camp, docks and yards at condominiums on Juno\nTrail and water breaches the sea wall at Blair's Jungle Den.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 8:30 PM EDT Sunday the stage was 2.9 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 2.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 8:30 PM EDT Sunday was 2.9 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise to 3.3 feet early this\nweek following a period of persistent northeasterly winds.\nAdditional rises are possible thereafter.\n- Flood stage is 2.3 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Monday afternoon at noon EDT.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSMLB"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS82 KMLB 190058"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KMLB.FL.W.0003.000000T0000Z-000000T0000Z/"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ec86a5b25822e52f8e371f554242bdd67483342f.001.1,2026-10-17T20:54:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7f1892302e6e287d1231cf4d12f60f419868b375.001.1,2026-10-17T09:04:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8aa4ca8f0a91b6616676b40340c36ef2b6f9788d.001.1,2026-10-16T21:21:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.dfc8045564b49517706a7715d068ca72ead6ebb3.001.1,2026-10-16T10:44:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7e5a6b135466609b1033d13cc0d52d1891c646cf.001.1,2026-10-15T21:36:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0102843d75ecf5c8efce3bbb90291fc98fa94c78.001.1,2026-10-15T15:34:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ece4802e04c97e36732b09ba56c6d3b0cce4d6b0.001.1,2026-10-15T08:56:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.011da60a226f747f480bb13e59db22de16ce56bc.00